1. version – Tells developers the current version of the project.

2. description – Tells developers the purpose or what the project 
is about.

3. main – Specifies the main entry-point file of the project.

4. scripts – Contains commands that can be executed using npm, 
such as starting or running the project.

5. dependencies – Contains the packages or libraries required for 
the application to work properly.

6. devDependencies – Contains packages used during development,
such as tools for testing, debugging, and automatically restarting 
the application.

What is the node_modules folder, and why is it not included when you submit or share a project?
The node_modules folder stores all the packages and libraries 
installed in a Node.js project. It is not included when submitting 
or sharing a project because it can contain many files and take up 
a lot of storage. Instead, developers share the package.json and
package-lock.json files so that others can install the required 
packages by running npm install